          "content": "131"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.146,
            0.535,
            0.188
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{-1}{\\tan \\theta - \\sec \\theta} = \\frac{1}{\\sec \\theta - \\tan \\theta}",
          "image_source": "images/page_18_equation_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.202,
            0.658,
            0.221
          ],
          "content": "which is the RHS of the identity, we are required to prove."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.408,
            0.246,
            0.59,
            0.265
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "EXERCISE 8.3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.276,
            0.784,
            0.294
          ],
          "content": "1. Express the trigonometric ratios sin A, sec A and tan A in terms of cot A."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.3,
            0.708,
            0.318
          ],
          "content": "2. Write all the other trigonometric ratios of $\\angle \\mathrm { A }$ in terms of sec A."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.323,
            0.805,
            0.388
          ],
          "content": "3. Choose the correct option. Justify your choice. (i) 9 $\\sec^{2}A - 9\\tan^{2}A =$ (A) 1 (B) 9 (C) 8 (D) 0"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.393,
            0.812,
            0.435
          ],
          "content": "(ii) (1 + tan θ + sec θ) (1 + cot θ − cosec θ) = (A) 0 (B) 1 (C) 2 (D) -1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.44,
            0.843,
            0.483
          ],
          "content": "(iii) (sec A + tan A) (1 − sin A) = (A) sec A (B) sin A (C) cosec A (D) cos A"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.159,
            0.493,
            0.846,
            0.566
          ],
          "content": "(iv) $\\frac{1 + \\tan^{2}\\mathrm{A}}{1 + \\cot^{2}\\mathrm{A}}$ (A) $\\sec ^ { 2 } \\mathbf { A }$ (B) -1 $\\cot ^ { 2 } \\mathrm { A }$ (D) $\\tan ^ { 2 } \\mathbf { A }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.57,
            0.899,
            0.663
          ],
          "content": "4. Prove the following identities, where the angles involved are acute angles for which the expressions are defined. (i) $( \\csc \\theta - \\cot \\theta ) ^ { 2 } = { \\frac { 1 - \\cos \\theta } { 1 + \\cos \\theta } }$ (ii) $\\frac{\\cos  A }{1 + \\sin  A } + \\frac{1 + \\sin  A }{\\cos  A } = 2 \\sec  A$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.668,
            0.568,
            0.707
          ],
          "content": "(iii) $\\frac{\\tan \\theta}{1 - \\cot \\theta} + \\frac{\\cot \\theta}{1 - \\tan \\theta} = 1 + \\sec \\theta$ cosec θ"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.712,
            0.688,
            0.73
          ],
          "content": "[Hint : Write the expression in terms of sin θ and cos θ]"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.734,
            0.812,
            0.773
          ],
          "content": "(iv) $\\frac{1 + \\sec A}{\\sec A} = \\frac{\\sin^{2}A}{1 - \\cos A}$ [Hint : Simplify LHS and RHS separately]"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.776,
            0.898,
            0.865
          ],
          "content": "(v) $\\frac{\\cos^{-}A-\\sin A+1}{\\cos A+\\sin A-1}=\\csc\\mathrm{A}+\\cot\\mathrm{A}$ , using the identity cosec² $\\mathrm { A }   =   1 + \\cot ^ { 2 } \\mathrm { A }$ (vi) $\\sqrt{\\frac{1 + \\sin A}{1 - \\sin A}} = \\sec A + \\tan A$ (vii) $\\frac{\\sin \\theta - 2\\sin^{3}\\theta}{2\\cos^{3}\\theta - \\cos \\theta} = \\tan \\theta$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.873,
            0.703,
            0.892
          ],
          "content": "(viii) $(\\sin \\mathrm{A} + \\csc \\mathrm{c} \\mathrm{A})^2 + (\\cos \\mathrm{A} + \\sec \\mathrm{A})^2 = 7 + \\tan^2 \\mathrm{A} + \\cot^2 \\mathrm{A}$"
        },
        {
